The arm64 guards accept the compiler spelling too (aarch64 port, task A4)

Sixty-nine dispatch headers test __arm64__, which Apple compilers define but an
aarch64-linux host clang does not: it says __aarch64__. Every #if line that tests
__arm64__ gains the second spelling. Guest compiles define both and do not change;
host tools (migcom first, via mach/boolean.h) stop dying on "architecture not
supported". Extends 0018, which fixed the one header darling PR 1753 had fixed.

